```

This check is at line 130-131. But `*buf = p` and `*taglen = len` are set at lines 127-128, BEFORE this check. So even if the check fails and the function returns an error, `*taglen` is already set to `len`.

But in `print_tags_recursive`, the code checks:
```c
r = sc_asn1_read_tag(&tagp, bytesleft, &cla, &tag, &len);
if (r != SC_SUCCESS || tagp == NULL) {
    printf("Error in decoding.\n");
    return;
}
```

So if `sc_asn1_read_tag` returns an error, `print_tags_recursive` returns early. The `len` value is not used. So this is safe.

